avatars-title = People and contact pictures
avatars-mode = Sender and contact pictures
avatars-off = Hide pictures
avatars-initials = Generate initials locally
avatars-contacts = Use local contact pictures, with initials as fallback
avatars-help = Initials are generated on this device. Contact pictures use only embedded PNG or JPEG photos already saved in your own address books, up to 512 × 512 pixels and 128 KiB. Remote picture URLs and external avatar services are never requested. This preference is saved with your account and can be held by your administrator.
avatars-default = Restore inherited preference
avatars-sender-icons = Show bundled sender-domain icons
avatars-sender-icons-help = Recognised social, developer, AI, shopping and government domains use icons bundled with this app. Your own contact pictures take priority. Unknown senders use locally generated initials with 192 colours. Icons are domain hints, not proof that a message is authentic. No external logo service is contacted.
avatars-icons-default = Restore inherited icon preference
avatars-brand-avatars = Show brand logos beside verified senders
avatars-brand-avatars-help = In the reader, a recognised company shows its logo beside the sender only when the message passed DKIM and an aligned DMARC check for that company's own domain. Otherwise the normal avatar is used. Logos are bundled with this app; nothing is requested from the sender.
avatars-brand-avatars-default = Restore inherited brand logo preference
avatars-domain-icon = { $name } domain icon · sender identity is not verified by this icon
avatars-unverified-sender = Unverified sender · no brand icon is shown because this message did not pass the authentication check
avatars-require-auth = Authentication needed for brand logos
avatars-require-auth-help = Choose when a recognised company's logo may replace the initials beside a sender. Never: show it whenever the sender's domain matches. Only if a check failed (default): show it unless the message failed DKIM or DMARC. Always: show it only when the message passed DKIM and an aligned DMARC check for that company's own domain, so mail not yet checked shows initials. The domain match includes subdomains such as mail.example.com. This preference is saved with your account and can be held by your administrator.
avatars-require-auth-never = Never (match on domain only)
avatars-require-auth-known-failure = Only if a check failed
avatars-require-auth-always = Always (require a passed check)
avatars-require-auth-default = Restore inherited authentication preference
avatars-favorites-first = Show favorite contacts first in recipient suggestions
avatars-favorites-first-help = Contacts you starred are listed ahead of other matches when you type a recipient. Only the order changes; no suggestion is hidden.
avatars-favorites-first-default = Restore inherited favorites preference
